# Learn more https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files

# dependencies
node_modules/

# Expo
.expo/
dist/
web-build/
expo-env.d.ts

# Native
ios/
*.orig.*
*.jks

# `User App/android/` is deliberately NOT ignored — the native project is
# committed, because it carries hand-edits that `expo prebuild` would destroy
# (the release signingConfig, and the long-path ninja the Windows build needs).
# Its own android/.gitignore keeps build/, .gradle/ and .cxx/ out.
#
# Two things inside it must still never be committed, and are listed here
# rather than in that file so they stay excluded no matter what a prebuild
# rewrites: the upload key (covered by `*.jks` above) and the Gradle properties
# holding its passwords in plaintext. The passwords' proper home is the
# user-level ~/.gradle/gradle.properties, outside the repo entirely.
User App/android/gradle.properties
*.p8
*.p12
*.key
*.mobileprovision

# Metro
.metro-health-check*

# debug
npm-debug.*
yarn-debug.*
yarn-error.*

# macOS
.DS_Store
*.pem

# local env files
.env*.local

# typescript
*.tsbuildinfo
.vercel

.env

# Google Analytics / Google Cloud service-account keys — never commit these,
# wherever in the repo one ends up.
*service-account*.json
*service_account*.json
lampose-analytics*.json
